\begin_layout Title
\begin_inset Formula $\mathrm{SPMe^{+}}$
\end_inset


\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

An Enhanced Single-Particle Model with Solid Stoichiometry Correction
\end_layout

\begin_layout Author
Wes Hileman
\end_layout

\begin_layout Date
4 March 2026
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section*
Overview
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
We have constructed Physics-Informed Machine-Learning (PIML) models for lithium batteries by combining the SPMe with neural networks (NNs) or Gaussian processes (GPs)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
These models are accurate at high C-rate,
 even for cells with thick electrodes,
 but the NNs or GPs add a lot of complexity in terms of parameters and computation
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Can we develop a model with fewer machine-learning (ML) elements that is still accurate at high C-rate?
\end_layout

