\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Idea:
 Let's construct a time-variant IIR filter with this dc gain to estimate 
\begin_inset Formula $\bar{\theta}_{\mathrm{s}}(\tilde{x})$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Problem:
 We don't have an expression for a time constant for the filter
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Solution:
 Assume log cubic spline interpolation over a number of control points for the time constant,
 and regress the control points by comparison to the full-order PDAE model
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
In the end,
 we have an IIR filter with a time-varying time constant 
\begin_inset Formula $\tau(\theta_{\mathrm{avg}}[k])$
\end_inset

 and time-varying dc gain 
\begin_inset Formula $\bar{\theta}_{\mathrm{s,dc}}(\theta_{\mathrm{avg}}[k])$
\end_inset

 that computes 
\begin_inset Formula $\bar{\theta}_{\mathrm{s}}(\tilde{x})$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
\begin_inset Formula $a[k]=\exp(-t_{\mathrm{s}}/\tau(\theta_{\mathrm{avg}}[k]))$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Four different configurations for the LTV filter's 
\begin_inset Formula $b$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $c$
\end_inset

 coefficients,
 we will try them all:
